{
 "arc": [
  {
   "slide": 1,
   "title": "The BeanBox Opportunity",
   "point": "BeanBox has proven product-market fit in Kyiv’s competitive specialty coffee market, achieving 400 paying subscribers in just 6 months, and is raising 300k EUR to scale production via a second roastery.",
   "evidence": [
    "f1",
    "f2",
    "f5",
    "f7"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 2,
   "title": "Market Resilience & Demand",
   "point": "The Kyiv specialty coffee sector is growing and resilient, with consumers demonstrating a willingness to pay premium prices for high-quality, fresh-roast delivery despite economic challenges.",
   "evidence": [
    "f16",
    "f18",
    "f15"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 3,
   "title": "Competitive Landscape",
   "point": "While the market is active with established players like Kyiv City Roast and Idealist Coffee, these competitors validate the subscription model and highlight the demand for fresh, specialized coffee.",
   "evidence": [
    "f9",
    "f17",
    "f19",
    "f12"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 4,
   "title": "Product & Traction",
   "point": "BeanBox delivers a premium subscription at 18 EUR/month, achieving rapid initial traction of approximately 67 new subscribers per month, driven by strong product quality.",
   "evidence": [
    "f3",
    "f2",
    "f11",
    "f1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 5,
   "title": "Financial Snapshot",
   "point": "The business generates stable Monthly Recurring Revenue (MRR) of 7,200 EUR, calculated from 400 paying subscribers at 18 EUR per month, demonstrating early unit economics viability.",
   "evidence": [
    "f4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 6,
   "title": "The Founding Team",
   "point": "The founding team combines deep technical expertise in roasting with specialized skills in growth marketing, creating a balanced capability for both product excellence and customer acquisition.",
   "evidence": [
    "f6"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 7,
   "title": "The Ask & Use of Funds",
   "point": "We are raising 300k EUR in seed funding, specifically allocated to open a second roastery to increase production capacity and support future growth.",
   "evidence": [
    "f7",
    "f8"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 8,
   "title": "Why This Works Now",
   "point": "With proven traction and a clear path to scaling production, BeanBox is positioned to capture a larger share of Kyiv’s growing specialty coffee market by meeting increased demand.",
   "evidence": [
    "f5",
    "f18",
    "f19"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "why": "This deck structure persuades seed investors by leading with the strongest proof point: rapid traction (400 subs in 6 months). It validates the market context early to show the opportunity is real, then introduces the competitive landscape to acknowledge risks honestly. It highlights the team's complementary skills as the engine behind the traction, presents the financials as a simple, verifiable calculation, and ends with a clear, specific use of funds (second roastery) that directly addresses the bottleneck to scaling. This order builds confidence in the team and product before asking for capital."
}
